  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Gradual clearing today with dry conditions expected to\npersist through at least Thursday. Increasing thunderstorm\nchances again by the weekend and into early next week, along \nwith hot and humid conditions.\n\nA cold front is currently working its way across the forecast\narea this afternoon. A few thunderstorms and heavier downpours\nwill continue along this front for a few more hours, eventually\nmoving east and out of the area by early evening. Behind the \nfront, skies will gradually clear and a drier airmass featuring \nless humid conditions will follow. This drier airmass will\nremain in place through at least Thursday. Lows on Wednesday\nmorning will feel a little chilly...mountains fall into the\nupper 40s/low 50s and mid 50s east of the mountains.\n\nUpper ridging will build by late week and into early next week\nas the pattern begins to flip towards above normal temperatures.\nAlong with this warming pattern comes a chance of daily \nafternoon/evening storms beginning as early as Friday. Heat will\nbuild each day, with the potential for upper 80s to upper 90s \nby Mon/Tue. The ridge will likely continue to intensify through\nmuch of next week, so expect hot and humid conditions to\npersist.",
